%% Module 5: Human-in-the-Loop — Read vs Write Trust Separation
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User/Agent
    participant O as Orchestrator
    participant G as Guardrail Service
    participant Q as Escalation Queue
    participant H as Human Reviewer
    participant A as Action Executor
    participant L as Audit Log

    U->>O: Query / requested action
    O->>G: Evaluate response (Module 4 scores)

    alt Read action, high confidence
        G-->>O: Auto-approved
        O->>U: Response delivered immediately
        O->>L: Log (auto-approved, no human)
    else Read action, low confidence
        G-->>O: Needs review
        O->>Q: Enqueue draft_answer, reason, timestamp
        Q->>H: Notify reviewer
        H-->>Q: Approve / Reject (or timeout)
        alt Timeout — SLA breach
            Q->>O: Default to safe fallback response
            O->>L: Log (escalated, timed out, fallback used)
        else Reviewed in time
            Q->>O: Decision
            O->>U: Reviewed response delivered
            O->>L: Log (escalated, human decision recorded)
        end
    else Write action e.g. file claim, update account
        G->>O: Generate PROPOSED DIFF, not executed yet
        O->>U: Show diff, request confirmation
        U-->>O: Confirm / Reject
        alt Confirmed
            O->>A: Execute with idempotency key<br/>prevents double-execution on retry
            A-->>O: Execution result
            O->>L: Log (proposed, confirmed, executed)
        else Rejected
            O->>L: Log (proposed, rejected, not executed)
        end
    end
